# Ecom SEO — Cursor Agent project rules

## Source of truth
- Work in the existing repository `tarikk786786/ecom-seo`, branch `main`.
- Before changes, inspect the latest Git state and read `README.md`, `docs/MASTER_PRD.md`, `docs/API_INTEGRATION_CATALOG.md`, `docs/KEYWORD_RESEARCH_UI_SPEC.md`, `docs/AUTO_REQUIREMENT_DISCOVERY_PROMPT.md`, `BUILD_PROGRESS.md`, `FEATURE_STATUS.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md`, and `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Keep implementation modular and preserve existing behavior. Do not rebuild from scratch or duplicate frameworks/dependencies without evidence.
- The reference UI is the dense keyword workspace in `docs/KEYWORD_RESEARCH_UI_SPEC.md`.

## Implementation behavior
- Implement actual code, not only plans or more prompt documents, whenever the environment allows.
- Work in small, coherent cycles. Run relevant checks, start/refresh the actual preview, verify the affected flow, fix regressions, update project tracking documents, and commit/push each verified cycle.
- When the user says `NEXT`, inspect the latest repo state/progress and continue the highest-priority unfinished item. Do not restart or repeat completed work.
- Always report changed files, commands/tests actually run and their outcomes, real preview or reproducible launch instructions, remaining blockers, and the commit SHA/link after a push.

## Data integrity
- Never invent search volume, CPC, bid ranges, competition, ranking, prices, product availability, chart points, data freshness, provider links, or successful API states.
- Preserve provider, source URL/ID, geographic/language context, metric unit/definition/window, observation time, and retrieval time.
- Distinguish observed, derived, estimated and AI-generated results. Google Trends relative interest is not absolute search volume. Page views, social engagement and marketplace listing counts are not search volume.
- A provider may be shown as CONNECTED only after an authorized live request succeeds. A docs link, reachable URL, mocked test or configured key alone is not proof of a working live integration.
- Return partial results when some providers fail and show a truthful status per provider. Never substitute demo records into production result paths.

## API research and credentials
- For new/updated integrations, use current official docs, endpoint references, pricing, quota and terms. Verify the exact API product and keep affiliate, seller, public and account-owner APIs separate.
- Never bypass OAuth, account approval, paywalls, rate limits, CAPTCHAs or terms. Do not scrape browsers/cookies or unrelated files for secrets.
- Never print or commit secrets. Check only whether relevant expected environment variables are present; never echo their values. Put placeholder names only in `.env.example`.
- Do not buy credits, start paid subscriptions, deploy paid resources, run large billable jobs, delete data or apply destructive production migrations without explicit authorization.
- For unavailable credentials/approvals, finish safe independent implementation and clearly mark live verification blocked.

## Security and quality
- Keep privileged keys server-side; do not expose service-role keys, private API keys, payment secrets or tokens in browser bundles, logs or Git.
- Preserve tenant authorization, Supabase RLS, minimal permissions, provider licensing/retention constraints, input validation, rate limiting, secret redaction and safe URL handling.
- Audit dependencies and use compatible pinned package versions and lockfiles.
- Run relevant typecheck, lint, unit/contract/integration tests and production build. Do not claim a command passed unless it actually ran.
- For meaningful UI changes, provide a real running preview or browser screenshot when available, check desktop/mobile layouts and functionality, and disclose if preview access is blocked.

## Git workflow
- Inspect `git status`, branch and remote HEAD before editing.
- Never overwrite unrelated user changes, discard uncommitted work, or force-push.
- Before committing, inspect the diff and run a secret scan.
- Commit with a specific message, push to `main`, and verify the remote commit. If a push fails, report the exact error; do not claim success.
- Keep `BUILD_PROGRESS.md`, `FEATURE_STATUS.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md`, and `ARCHITECTURE.md` accurate. Mark features TESTED or LIVE only when evidence exists.

## Canonical workflows
- For exhaustive API research/setup, execute `docs/AUTO_REQUIREMENT_DISCOVERY_PROMPT.md` and maintain `docs/API_REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX.md` and `docs/REQUIREMENTS_CHECKLIST.md`.
- For the keyword research UI, follow `docs/KEYWORD_RESEARCH_UI_SPEC.md`.
- For overall scope, follow `docs/MASTER_PRD.md`.
